<title>USA: Teamsters, UPS in tentative deal, sources say.</title>
<headline>Teamsters, UPS in tentative deal, sources say.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Intenational Brotherhood of Teamsters have reached a tentative agreement to end their 15-day strike against United Parcel Service, sources close to the talks said Monday.  </p>
<p>Labor Secretary Alexis Herman was to announce a breakthrough in the latest round of marathon contract talks that began Thursday at a 10:45 p.m. EDT (0245 GMT) news conference.</p>
<p>She was to appear with Ron Carey, president of the Teamsters, and a senior representative of UPS, the world's largest carrier of small packages.</p>
<p>The strike by 185,000 Teamsters has crippled UPS, costing it $650 million in lost business so far.</p>
</text>
